@startuml system-overview
!include ../../_plantuml/study-style.puml
title Phono 360 - what runs where (study map)

left to right direction

rectangle "Mic board: MEMS Interface v02" as MIC {
  component "4 x sensiBel SBM100B\noptical MEMS mics\nN / S / W / E, r = 61 mm" as MICS
  component "I2C2 sensors\nHDC2021 (T/RH)\nMMC5603NJ (mag)\nLSM6DSR (IMU)" as SENS
  component "STM32U575 (Zephyr)\n**SAI + GPDMA** capture\n**audio_dsp**: A/C/Z, Fast/Slow, Leq\n**fft_engine**: FFT, 1/3-oct, CSD\n**doa_***: SRP-PHAT, quality, cal\n**env_service**: orientation, tamper\nNVS settings, MCUboot" as STM
  MICS --> STM : I2S (SAI1_A + SAI1_B)\n48 kHz, 32-bit
  SENS --> STM : I2C
}

rectangle "LTE Node v04" as LTE {
  component "nRF9161 (NCS)\n**stm32uartmgr**: framing, link ACK\n**vimms_phono**: frames -> VimmsSound2\n**vimms_pudding_cmd**: cloud commands\nSTM32 FOTA, UTC time relay" as NRF
}

cloud "MQTT broker\n(TLS)" as BROKER
rectangle "Cloud backend\n+ Kalibrator (browser)" as APPS

STM <--> NRF : **phonocom**\nUART 1 Mbaud\n0xAA 0x55 frames
NRF <--> BROKER : LTE-M\nProtobuf over MQTT
BROKER <--> APPS : telemetry,\ncommands

legend right
  Source: Phono360/fw/README.md @ d49d732,
  vimms-engineering docs/phono-360 (lte-node-firmware.md, hardware.md).
  Simplified for study; see the VIMMS Engineering Docs for the full diagrams.
endlegend
@enduml
